[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Eurobot Rules

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @eurobot

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Each node below paraphrases a clause of the Eurobot competition rules.
None of it is the verbatim rule text. The converter from
``developer/tasks/eurobot/20260827_eurobot_rules_import`` replaces this
document with clauses extracted from the official rules PDF.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Robot

[RULE]
UID: RULE-4.1
TITLE: Robot footprint
STATEMENT: >>>
The robot's footprint at the start of the match shall not exceed a
perimeter of 1200 mm.
<<<

[RULE]
UID: RULE-4.2
TITLE: Robot height
STATEMENT: >>>
The robot shall not exceed a height of 350 mm, excluding the beacon
support.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Safety

[RULE]
UID: RULE-5.1
TITLE: Emergency stop
STATEMENT: >>>
The robot shall carry a red emergency stop button, reachable without
touching any other part of the robot, that cuts power to every actuator.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Match

[RULE]
UID: RULE-6.1
TITLE: Match duration
STATEMENT: >>>
A match lasts 100 seconds. The robot shall operate autonomously for the
whole match, without any human intervention after the start.
<<<

[RULE]
UID: RULE-7.1
TITLE: Score estimate
STATEMENT: >>>
Before the match starts, the team shall announce the score it expects to
reach. A correct estimate earns bonus points.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]
